  "prompt": "You are working alone in this directory. It holds a client's asset pack; its README.md lists what is in it. Make the video that the brief below describes. Nobody will answer questions, so make your own decisions and see it through to the end. There is no web access. Deliver the finished video as `deliverable.mp4` in this directory.\n\nMake it with Montagent, the video editor: its MCP server is connected, and the `montagent` CLI is on your PATH.\n\n---\n\n# Change request on brief C: the owl says it slower\n\n**About 9 seconds \u00b7 1920\u00d71080 \u00b7 30 fps \u00b7 16:9.** Deliver one MP4 with sound.\n\nThis directory already holds the finished owl short from brief C. `hoot.montagent.json` is its\nproject, built from `hoot.base.json` and `hoot.spec.json`. The original brief's beats and\nacceptance checklist still hold, apart from the one change below.\n\n## The change\n\nThe client says the owl talks too fast. Slow the voice line to **85 % of its speed** without\nchanging its pitch, and keep everything in step with the slower words: the beak, the wave on\n\"Hi\u2026 Hoot\", the card and the gesture on \"\u2026as a file\", the picture change on \"movie\", and the\nlockup and cheer after the line. The video may run longer to fit; nothing else should change.",
